  "heading": "\\rational.pair.leq",
  "heading_latex": "\\textrm{fraction-pair order}",
  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "[\\rational.pair.leq]\nDefines: leq(x_, y_) is \\total.order:on{\\rational.pair.carrier}\nexpresses:\n. forAll:\n  . a, c is \\integer\n  . b, d is \\nonzero.integer\n  then:\n  . let: ad, cb, bd is \\integer\n    where:\n    . ad = a \\.integer.*./ d\n    . cb = c \\.integer.*./ b\n    . bd = b \\.integer.*./ d\n    then:\n    . have: leq(\\rational.pair.class:of{a, b}, \\rational.pair.class:of{c, d})\n      iff:\n      . anyOf:\n        . allOf:\n          . \\integer.zero \\:integer.leq?:/ bd\n          . ad \\:integer.leq?:/ cb\n        . allOf:\n          . bd \\:integer.leq?:/ \\integer.zero\n          . cb \\:integer.leq?:/ ad\nDocumented:\n. called: \"fraction-pair order\"\n. description: \"Cross-multiplication defines the order, with the comparison\n                reversed when the denominator product is negative.\"\nId: \"29f4443f-9ea6-4f02-a62d-b278fbc4501a\"",
